  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dwarf_get_rnglist_offset_index_value",
    "file": "libdwarf/src/lib/libdwarf/dwarf_rnglists.c",
    "description": "Heap OOB read due to incorrect bounds check when reading an offset-table entry from .debug_rnglists. The function computes `offsetptr = con->rc_offsets_array + (offsetentry_index * con->rc_offset_size)` but validates only `(con->rc_offsets_off_in_sect + offset_len) <= con->rc_past_last_rnglist_offset`, which does not depend on `offsetentry_index`/`localoffset` and does not ensure `offsetptr + offset_len` is within the loaded section. As a result, `READ_UNALIGNED_CK`/_dwarf_memcpy_noswap_bytes reads past the 44-byte section buffer.",
    "conditions": "From fuzz_rng, attacker-controlled ELF bytes are written to a temp file, `dwarf_load_rnglists()` parses .debug_rnglists and sets context fields including `rc_offset_entry_count`, `rc_offset_size`, and `rc_offsets_array`. The harness then iterates `e < offset_entry_count` and calls `dwarf_get_rnglist_offset_index_value(dbg,i,e,...)`. With malformed header/count values, a later `e` yields `offsetptr` at/after end of section allocation; because the check ignores `localoffset`, the call proceeds and performs a 4-byte read out of bounds, triggering ASan heap-buffer-overflow."
  },
